The user is asking if the formatting of the example message from the external team is correct. Let me compare it to what we generated and the proto schema.

Looking at the external team's example:
```
ProvidersMenu {  
  subsystems: [    
    ProviderSubsystemMenu {      
      provider_urn: "machine_controls"      
      provider_type: eMachinePositioning      
      provider_display_name: "Machine Controls"      
      menu_items: [        
        ProviderMenuItem { display_text: "Machine Overview",        url: "https://www.google.com" }        
        ProviderMenuItem { display_text: "Autos Setup",             url: "https://www.google.com" }        
        ...
      ]    
    }    
    ProviderSubsystemMenu {      
      ...
    }  
  ]
}
```

And what we generated:
```
ProvidersMenu {
  subsystems {
    provider_urn: "urn:ctct:independentlib:providermenu-1"
    provider_type: 1
    provider_display_name: "Machine Positioning"
    menu_items {
      display_text: "Machine Positioning Feature 1"
      url: "https://localhost:8080/provider/1/feature/1"
    }
    menu_items {
      display_text: "Machine Positioning Feature 2"
      url: "https://localhost:8080/provider/1/feature/2"
    }
  }
  ...
}
```

The key differences:
1. **Array syntax**: They use `subsystems: [...]` while we use repeated fields with multiple `subsystems { }` blocks
2. **Menu items**: They use `menu_items: [ ProviderMenuItem { ... } ProviderMenuItem { ... } ]` while we use repeated `menu_items { }` blocks

Actually, both are valid protobuf text formats! Protobuf has two text representations:


- **Debug string format** (what `DebugString()` produces): uses repeated field syntax like `field { } field { }`
- **Protobuf text format** (what can be read back): uses array syntax like `field: [{ }, { }]` or repeated `field { }`

However, there's an issue with their formatting - the `ProviderMenuItem` objects are all on one line without proper nesting. Let me look closer:

```
menu_items: [        
  ProviderMenuItem { display_text: "Machine Overview",        url: "https://www.google.com" }
```

This is syntactically valid protobuf text, though the inline formatting makes it less readable. Both representations are acceptable—theirs uses the bracket array notation while ours uses the repeated field blocks, which are functionally equivalent in protobuf.

